    {
      "id": "sla-escalation-monitoring",
      "name": "SLA clocks, at-risk flags and escalation",
      "story": "As an approver, every ready case runs an SLA clock from the moment completeness passed — 48/24/8 business hours by band — and a recurring evaluator flags a case AT RISK to me at 80% consumed, records a breach permanently once the window passes, and steps unactioned high-risk cases up the chain from compliance officer to Head of Financial Crime to COO, with every notification persisted as an addressable record naming recipient and time; the worklist shows SLA remaining and AT RISK / breached flags at a glance, and no SLA pressure ever unlocks a shortcut past approval. Seeded cases SEED-ATRISK-004 (Vantage Metals Ltd, 87.5% of its window consumed) and SEED-BREACH-005 (Ridgeline Capital Ltd, past due) exercise the evaluator.",
